# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the InterMux website following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 to project dependencies
- **Package Manager**: npm (used package-lock.json)
- **Status**: Successfully installed with 349 packages added

### 2. Code Configuration
- **Modified File**: `website/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag in the root layout
  - Preserved all existing code structure and metadata

### 3. Files Modified
- `website/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `website/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `website/app/layout.tsx` - Integrated Analytics component

## Implementation Details

This is a Next.js 16.4.3 App Router project, so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) as per the official Vercel documentation for App Router projects.

The Analytics component is placed at the end of the `<body>` tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with the main content rendering, following Vercel's recommended best practices.

## Testing & Verification

✅ **Linting**: Passed with no errors (`npm run lint`)
✅ **Build**: Successfully compiled with Next.js (`npm run build`)
✅ **TypeScript**: Type checking completed successfully
✅ **Static Generation**: All 8 pages generated without issues

## Next Steps

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the website to Vercel (or ensure it's already deployed)
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section for this project
3. Analytics will automatically begin tracking visitor data after deployment

## Notes

- The implementation uses the framework-specific import from `@vercel/analytics/next` for optimal Next.js integration
- The Analytics component automatically handles route changes and page views
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- Analytics will only collect data when deployed to a Vercel environment
